1
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,010
[XYLO] Teoritta, we did it.

2
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,720
[TEORITTA] Yes, as all
surely knew we would.

3
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,350
I permit you to praise me

4
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,440
in honor
of our inevitable victory.

5
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,060
"You're a truly great goddess.

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:24,690
Excellent work today, Teoritta."

7
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:26,610
[scoffs]

8
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:28,740
Excellent work, Teoritta.

9
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:31,410
You really are a great goddess.

10
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:33,120
[Teoritta chuckles softly]

11
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:35,030
[XYLO] And you're not alone,
you know.

12
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:39,250
Wanting to be praised
for doing your job well.

13
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:40,830
I think we're all like that.

14
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,090
Some people
may want it so badly,

15
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,880
they're willing
to risk their lives for it.

16
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:51,470
Yes.

17
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,600
[♪ inspirational music playing]

18
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:06,360
[sighs]

19
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,990
-[groans]
-[Xylo grunts]

20
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:09,950
[IRI] Help!

21
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,870
Please help me. It's my dad!

22
00:01:12,910 --> 00:01:15,700
A monster got him.
He's hurt. [sobs]

23
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:18,000
[Xylo grunts] Someone else
to protect.

24
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,290
You stay here.

25
00:01:19,330 --> 00:01:21,540
-I can take care--
-Do not despair, small one.

26
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:22,960
Hey!

27
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,460
[TEORITTA] All will be well.

28
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,420
For you are now
under the protection

29
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,760
of the goddess Teoritta
and her valiant knight,

30
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,130
Xylo Forbartz.

31
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:32,550
Let's make haste
to find your father the aid

32
00:01:32,590 --> 00:01:33,680
that he needs.

33
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,850
First, may I ask your name?

34
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:39,350
[sobbing] My--
my name is Ir-- [groans]

35
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:41,640
[muffled] Oh, no!
Are you injured as well?

36
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,650
Teoritta!

37
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:47,730
[sword slashes]

38
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:50,900
[IRI] Die.

39
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:52,740
[sword clinks]

40
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,870
[grunts]

41
00:01:56,830 --> 00:01:58,240
[groans]

42
00:01:58,290 --> 00:01:59,330
[Xylo grunts]

43
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:03,460
[TSAV] Oh, whoopsies!
I just shot a kid, I think.

44
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,750
I mean, they're weird.

45
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:07,590
[VENETIM] Tsav! Please tell me

46
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:09,250
you did not just
kill a civilian!

47
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,380
[TSAV] It looked like she
was attacking Teoritta.

48
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:15,180
-Like I said, they're weird!
-[VENETIM] Weird? Try "insane"!

49
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:19,970
[Iri retches] I will not allow.

50
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,940
[Xylo grunts]

51
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,850
[Iri yells]

52
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:27,270
[gasps, grunts]

53
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:28,900
Teoritta!

54
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,110
-[panting]
-[XYLO] Are you hurt?

55
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:33,190
I told you that you
should stay back.

56
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:35,150
-Xylo.
-Yes?

57
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,240
It appears...

58
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,330
learning to use this
may prove a worthwhile endeavor.

59
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:42,410
Huh.

60
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:43,500
[sighs]

61
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
So that's how you
blocked its attack.

62
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,500
I'll have to buy you
an even better one, then.

63
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,340
And train you up.

64
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,130
We need to be careful.

65
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:56,340
A faerie disguising itself
as a human.

66
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:01,180
It might have been Spriggan
that ambushed us.

67
00:03:02,850 --> 00:03:05,270
I guess the Demon Blight
sees you as a threat.

68
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:07,060
One it would like to eliminate.

69
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:09,400
Good. I could want
for nothing more.

70
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,610
[scoffs]

71
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:17,030
You goddesses.

72
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:19,410
Never can make anything easy,
can you?

73
00:03:20,830 --> 00:03:22,410
Right. Back to the barracks,

74
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:24,250
and those good-for-nothing
bastards.

75
00:03:24,290 --> 00:03:27,620
Our allies. Let us now return
to their sides where we belong!

76
00:03:27,670 --> 00:03:30,130
-But before we go...
-Huh?

77
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:32,340
...you know what to do, yes?

78
00:03:33,090 --> 00:03:34,720
-Ah...
-[crackling]

79
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:35,970
Hmm.

80
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,890
Come, my knight!

81
00:03:37,930 --> 00:03:39,220
Say the words!

82
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,850
-[Xylo gasps]
-With utmost thoroughness

83
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:42,060
and gusto,

84
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,560
praise your brilliant goddess!

85
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:47,020
[indistinct chatter]

86
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:51,770
About 130 evacuees
have made it to the stronghold

87
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,190
and no fatalities.

88
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:54,860
I would say
that the Thirteenth Order

89
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:56,320
has done itself proud.

90
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,820
Captain Kivia has really whipped
us all into shape.

91
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,660
[SIENA] But I haven't seen her
or the infantry lieutenant

92
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:02,830
anywhere.

93
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:03,870
[Zofflec sighs]

94
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:07,120
Maybe they're letting us bask
in the spotlight for once.

95
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,000
They usually lead the charge.

96
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,290
We deserve a chance
to shine now and then.

97
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:12,750
[Siena sighs]

98
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:16,590
[MARLEN] You fought well today.
All of you.

99
00:04:17,010 --> 00:04:20,550
Let the military and the Temple
continue to work together...

100
00:04:20,590 --> 00:04:22,300
[FRENCI] Sorry
to keep you waiting.

101
00:04:22,350 --> 00:04:24,510
What did you learn? Tell me.

102
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,230
-[SOLDIER] Right!
-[MARLEN] Now, all units

103
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:27,680
return to your posts...

104
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:30,400
I'm afraid it appears
your suspicions were correct.

105
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,940
[both gasp]

106
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:40,240
[indistinct chatter]

107
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:49,290
[water splashing]

108
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,540
[Spriggan groans]

109
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:54,290
With these injuries,

110
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,130
I must focus on healing myself.

111
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:58,260
[grunts]

112
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:01,970
After that, a new host.

113
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:04,050
[grunts in pain]

114
00:05:05,510 --> 00:05:08,180
[RHYNO] Oh, look what the cat
dragged in.

115
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:10,310
I was hoping we'd cross paths.

116
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,730
Guess my wish came true.

117
00:05:15,770 --> 00:05:17,190
Huh, Spriggan?

118
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:18,490
[gasps]

119
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,160
Oh, dear. Don't tell me
you didn't know.

120
00:05:22,910 --> 00:05:24,950
Whenever a Demon Blight
is corrupting an area,

121
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:28,410
they give off a unique, uh,
what would you call it?

122
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:30,040
A unique wave, of sorts.

123
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,830
It's something
that other demon lords

124
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:32,960
can sense.

125
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,710
In fact,
that's how I was able

126
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:36,710
-to track you down.
-Wait.

127
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:38,170
[RHYNO] I'm not finished.

128
00:05:38,210 --> 00:05:39,550
Hear me out, won't you?

129
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:43,180
I happen to be a member
of the penal hero unit.

130
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:46,100
But you see, the crime
I am so very guilty of

131
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,270
is the simplest
and least offensive

132
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:49,680
of my comrades.

133
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,690
Guilt's a strange concept,
but I know I'm right.

134
00:05:52,730 --> 00:05:54,600
[Spriggan gasps]

135
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:57,400
[RHYNO] Can you guess my crime?

136
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,610
[gasps in fear]

137
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:07,910
Give up yet?

138
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:11,250
I love to kill my own kind.

139
00:06:11,290 --> 00:06:15,040
I take great pleasure in it.
It's just how I am.

140
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,290
[laughs]

141
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,920
Aren't humans great?

142
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:20,170
That trait is so common
among their kind,

143
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:23,090
they actually consider it
a rather boring motive.

144
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:25,220
-[laughs]
-Go away!

145
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,180
-I mean it! Get back!
-[RHYNO] Being boring

146
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,640
-is an amazing gift.
-Right now!

147
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,810
-[RHYNO] That's why...
-If you don't,

148
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:31,270
-you'll be sorry!
-[RHYNO]...I've completely

149
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:32,520
submitted to them.

150
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:34,520
I'll do pretty much anything
they ask of me.

151
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,310
-[screams]
-I'm currently learning

152
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,610
about ethics, you know,

153
00:06:37,650 --> 00:06:39,860
which is why
I see things clearly.

154
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,650
I realize,
from the Demons Blight's

155
00:06:41,690 --> 00:06:43,530
perspective,
I'm a homicidal maniac.

156
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,490
-[Spriggan screams]
-Slaughtering my own kind

157
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:47,620
for the thrill of it
makes me the most hackneyed,

158
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:50,120
cliched version of a murderer
you could imagine.

159
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,500
-[Spriggan screams]
-But in the eyes of humans,

160
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:54,500
I'm a brave champion for good.

161
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,540
Isn't it just baffling?
[chuckles]

162
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,170
To be honest,
I'm still trying to work out

163
00:06:58,210 --> 00:06:59,290
the logic behind it myself.

164
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:02,260
-Get away from me!
-Exhilarating!

165
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,630
Your screams
are music to my ears.

166
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:07,510
I am enamored with that sound.

167
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:11,220
Thrilling. Makes me
want to savor

168
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:12,470
-killing you.
-[thud]

169
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,230
[groans]

170
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:15,640
[RHYNO] Ah, how rude of me.

171
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:18,770
I've yet to introduce myself.

172
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:22,070
I am a Demon Lord, of course.

173
00:07:22,110 --> 00:07:23,360
Puck Puca.

174
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,440
Though naturally,
the humans call me

175
00:07:25,490 --> 00:07:27,570
by the name
of this body's original owner.

176
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,830
So I go by Rhyno these days.

177
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,870
Well, it's been fun.

178
00:07:33,910 --> 00:07:36,790
-Pleasant dreams, Spriggan.
-[Spriggan groans]

179
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:38,330
[splattering]

180
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,580
[thud]

181
00:07:46,470 --> 00:07:49,300
[BOOJUM] Quite impossible
to carry out my orders now.

182
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:52,600
It's starting to look like
I will have to disappoint

183
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,310
our king once more.

184
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,230
[bee buzzing]

185
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,600
[BOOJUM] Yes.

186
00:07:58,190 --> 00:08:00,860
I had a blood puppet
take my place in battle.

187
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:05,240
The Holy Sword
is far too dangerous.

188
00:08:06,070 --> 00:08:08,200
It's apparent
I'll need a great deal

189
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:10,530
of human blood
to kill those two.

190
00:08:10,570 --> 00:08:11,950
[distant rumbling]

191
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:18,830
[MARLEN] I heard
about your incredible deeds.

192
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,790
Truly valorous. I'm impressed.

193
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:24,460
[KIVIA] Thank you
for the praise.

194
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,970
You deserve commendation
as well.

195
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:28,260
I heard the rumors.

196
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:30,680
They say your leadership
was extraordinary.

197
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:32,760
It was merely good fortune.

198
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:36,100
Perhaps I was granted a blessing
from the saints of old.

199
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,640
There's no need to be humble.

200
00:08:38,690 --> 00:08:41,150
Your deeds will likely earn you
a position of leadership

201
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:42,230
among the High Priests.

202
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,570
If they see fit to bestow
upon me such an honor,

203
00:08:45,610 --> 00:08:47,740
I'll begin
with a staff overhaul.

204
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:51,280
As of now,
we are sorely lacking in unity.

205
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,910
Furthermore, Patausche,

206
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:55,490
I will promote you
to a position more befitting

207
00:08:55,530 --> 00:08:56,870
of your accomplishments.

208
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:06,090
A staff overhaul? I see.

209
00:09:06,590 --> 00:09:07,840
In truth,

210
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:09,670
we both know what that means.

211
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:12,010
You intend
to fill Temple leadership

212
00:09:12,050 --> 00:09:13,590
with coexisters.

213
00:09:14,850 --> 00:09:16,760
[distant thunderclap]

214
00:09:22,850 --> 00:09:25,480
[MARLEN] Did you interrogate
Lideo Sodrick?

215
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:29,030
I know the truth
about the coexister envoy

216
00:09:29,070 --> 00:09:30,200
he spoke of.

217
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,450
It was Mahaeyzel Zelkoff.

218
00:09:32,490 --> 00:09:36,120
All priests and Temple officials
invoke that name often.

219
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:39,660
They ask him for luck in battle.
How is that relevant?

220
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:41,830
Because in the inner lands
and elsewhere,

221
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:44,250
they pronounce the name
as "Zelkoof."

222
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:48,090
He called him ”Zelkoff,"
just like us northerners.

223
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:54,220
Someone with the funds
to hire the Adventurers Guild.

224
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,720
Someone born in the north
and involved with the Temple.

225
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:00,310
It certainly
narrows down the suspects.

226
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:02,940
Uncle,

227
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:05,110
when I was young,
I was desperate

228
00:10:05,150 --> 00:10:06,650
to experience the world.

229
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:09,820
You alone
opened the door for me.

230
00:10:10,690 --> 00:10:11,740
[MARLEN] Hmm.

231
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:14,200
When I chose to cut my own path,

232
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:17,740
to live a life wholly distinct
from that of my parents,

233
00:10:19,330 --> 00:10:22,370
you gave me everything
I needed to succeed,

234
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:24,370
including this sword.

235
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,750
[inaudible]

236
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:30,800
Remember sneaking me out
into the city?

237
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:33,970
You used the same alias
every time.

238
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:35,970
Always "Zelkoff."

239
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,310
You still remember that?

240
00:10:39,350 --> 00:10:41,600
Those memories are precious.

241
00:10:41,890 --> 00:10:43,020
That said,

242
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:45,810
I also made sure
to check your activity records.

243
00:10:45,850 --> 00:10:48,360
Take this recent battle,
for example.

244
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,780
The unit that first reported
the presence of faeries

245
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:52,070
in the Inland District.

246
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:54,990
I asked which one it was,

247
00:10:55,410 --> 00:10:57,950
and you told me seven, one,
one, zero.

248
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:02,790
Imagine my surprise
that no such unit exists.

249
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:07,420
[MARLEN] You never cease
to amaze me.

250
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,040
Hmm.

251
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,210
[grunts]

252
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:13,550
Why, Uncle?

253
00:11:14,050 --> 00:11:16,340
Why would you agree
to work with the coexisters?

254
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:21,180
For the sake of the people
I hold dear to me.

255
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,020
-[Rajit gasps]
-I order you to remain

256
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:24,140
where you are!

257
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,400
[MARLEN] I did it for myself

258
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:29,560
-and for my family.
-Uncle!

259
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,940
[MARLEN] And of course,

260
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:35,690
for the devout followers
of the Temple.

261
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:38,320
I want to save them all.

262
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:39,740
[Kivia grunts]

263
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:41,990
[MARLEN] Patausche.

264
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:47,080
Humanity will lose this battle.

265
00:11:47,710 --> 00:11:49,040
If nothing else,

266
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:53,880
I want to protect the righteous
of heart and my beloved family.

267
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,010
There is no other way.

268
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:57,300
[KIVIA] Hmm.

269
00:11:57,590 --> 00:11:58,640
How kind.

270
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:01,050
Unless you're not family

271
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,350
-or a follower--
-[MARLEN] The rest are none

272
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:03,520
of my concern.

273
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,470
[gasps]

274
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:07,850
[MARLEN] That's just
human nature. Is it not?

275
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:11,400
Or do you wish to be the sort
of high-minded paragon

276
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,480
who saves complete strangers,

277
00:12:13,530 --> 00:12:15,610
even at the cost
of her own family?

278
00:12:15,650 --> 00:12:17,610
You're wrong, Uncle!
I want to be--

279
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:20,160
[MARLEN] You're still
that naive, little girl

280
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:23,490
who never lost
her idealistic immaturity.

281
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:26,950
Patausche, it is time
to grow up.

282
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:29,250
Fight for what matters,

283
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:31,590
such as your family
and those close to you.

284
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:34,710
Help me shape the world

285
00:12:34,750 --> 00:12:36,050
as a coexister.

286
00:12:36,670 --> 00:12:38,970
Together, you and I
will act as the shepherds

287
00:12:39,010 --> 00:12:40,640
of our dear flock.

288
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,180
Please! Don't you see that--

289
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:43,970
[MARLEN] Nothing
can save humanity

290
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:45,390
from the Demon Blight.

291
00:12:45,850 --> 00:12:48,850
We'll be among the select few
with authority

292
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:51,770
that will allow us
to guide the survivors.

293
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:53,570
They'll be relying on us,

294
00:12:53,610 --> 00:12:55,320
and so we must lead them
down the--

295
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:56,860
Not another word!

296
00:12:57,650 --> 00:12:59,070
[♪ pensive music playing]

297
00:13:00,070 --> 00:13:01,280
[Kivia sobs]

298
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,910
[KIVIA] I'm sorry. Truly.

299
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:12,460
I always looked up to you
as my hero.

300
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,380
I mean that
from the bottom of my heart!

301
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:17,960
[continues sobbing]

302
00:13:19,220 --> 00:13:20,680
Why are you crying?

303
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,970
[Kivia sobs]

304
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,850
[KIVIA] I'm not like you.

305
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:27,470
Even those who have nothing
to do with me.

306
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:30,640
Strangers with names
and faces, I'll never know.

307
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:33,560
I can't abandon them.

308
00:13:34,110 --> 00:13:35,520
It's wrong!

309
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:39,820
That mindset is unusual
and self-righteous.

310
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,320
It's most disheartening.

311
00:13:42,490 --> 00:13:44,410
Perhaps a savior complex
stemming

312
00:13:44,450 --> 00:13:46,530
from an overinflated ego.

313
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,830
Suppose I only have
myself to blame

314
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:50,750
-for raising you that way.
-[KIVIA] That's enough!

315
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:53,370
-Rajit, arrest him!
-Right!

316
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:57,040
[sobbing] Uncle.

317
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:59,090
You must atone--

318
00:13:59,670 --> 00:14:00,760
[Rajit gasps]

319
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:02,970
-[buzzing]
-[gasps]

320
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,520
-[RAJIT] Captain, move!
-[splattering]

321
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,390
[Kivia exclaims]

322
00:14:10,430 --> 00:14:12,140
[rain pouring]

323
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,940
[MARLEN] Hmm.

324
00:14:24,410 --> 00:14:27,580
[Kivia screams]

325
00:14:32,210 --> 00:14:34,120
[MARLEN] I hope
you can forgive me,

326
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:35,330
Patausche.

327
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:38,550
I truly thought
of you as a daughter.

328
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:42,130
How disappointing.

329
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:47,050
[inaudible]

330
00:15:06,950 --> 00:15:08,320
[sword clinks]

331
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:12,500
[MALE PRIEST 1] Please hurry.
Something's wrong!

332
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:14,040
-High Priest!
-[all gasp]

333
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:24,300
[both gasp]

334
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:40,770
[XYLO] I take it Rhyno
isn't back yet?

335
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:43,780
Kivia will be pissed
if she finds out.

336
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:45,320
Unbelievable!

337
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:48,360
You've got to put that moron
on a chain already, Venetim.

338
00:15:48,410 --> 00:15:51,990
Really? That's pretty rich
coming from you, Jayce.

339
00:15:52,030 --> 00:15:54,250
You should lighten up.
What's so wrong

340
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:56,000
with letting him
do his own thing out there?

341
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,000
[sighs]

342
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:58,830
Maybe he's off
looting the wreckage.

343
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,250
Or found some faerie
to mess with for a laugh.

344
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:04,300
I've seen that guy
bring whole faeries back alive,

345
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:05,670
never to be seen again.

346
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:07,550
Right?

347
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:08,840
-Dotta?
-[DOTTA] Right.

348
00:16:08,890 --> 00:16:10,970
He said he's studying them
or something, I think.

349
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:12,100
[Xylo grunts]

350
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:13,970
[Dotta exclaims] Xylo!

351
00:16:14,010 --> 00:16:15,060
Perfect!

352
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:17,140
Don't forget to save some
for me, bro!

353
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,650
-[Xylo sighs]
-[NORGALLE] Colossal fool!

354
00:16:18,730 --> 00:16:22,980
You dare demand a reward
after such inaction? Not today!

355
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:24,020
You and Rhyno have much

356
00:16:24,070 --> 00:16:25,360
-to answer for.
-What?

357
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,360
Are you kidding?
I saved the goddess!

358
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,820
That's gotta be worth a sip

359
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:30,660
-or two.
-Who gives a damn?

360
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,160
-Just let it go already.
-[Neely snorts]

361
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,490
-[steps approaching]
-Huh?

362
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:37,910
-[FRENCI] Xylo.
-[horse neighs]

363
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,080
[XYLO] Frenci?

364
00:16:40,710 --> 00:16:43,380
You are always such a mess.
Care to explain

365
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:44,880
why you're sitting
on your laurels?

366
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,300
We're off duty.

367
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:47,840
You'll have to come back
tomorrow.

368
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,550
[TSAV] If you
are not gonna drink, gimme.

369
00:16:49,590 --> 00:16:50,590
[Xylo grunts]

370
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,810
I'm not in the mood
to take your abuse anyway.

371
00:16:53,850 --> 00:16:55,180
How pathetic.

372
00:16:55,770 --> 00:16:58,020
And you expect
to become a Mastibolt?

373
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:01,150
You're like a hot springs monkey
in hibernation.

374
00:17:01,190 --> 00:17:04,360
Can I get a moment to relax?
The battle has been settled.

375
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:06,230
Perhaps.

376
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:10,110
Unless the attack
on this city was a diversion.

377
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:11,410
Uh. [gasps]

378
00:17:13,030 --> 00:17:14,280
Hold on.

379
00:17:14,330 --> 00:17:15,700
Are you saying--

380
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,750
[FRENCI] Demon Blight Abaddon.

381
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:21,170
Its forces breached
the Ninth Order's defenses

382
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,380
and attacked the Second Capital.

383
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,550
-[gasps]
-[Norgalle shivers]

384
00:17:26,090 --> 00:17:29,630
[NORGALLE] My capital city
attacked by the faeries?

385
00:17:29,670 --> 00:17:32,720
And I wasn't there
to lead. To fight.

386
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:35,640
[FRENCI] They got wind
of our plans in advance

387
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,560
and deftly outmaneuvered us.

388
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,310
You mean...

389
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,890
[FRENCI] Yes.

390
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:42,560
The Second Capital

391
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:44,310
has fallen.

392
00:17:47,530 --> 00:17:49,150
[ADHIFF] Second Capital Zeyllent

393
00:17:49,190 --> 00:17:51,530
is the symbol
of the Federated Kingdom

394
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:54,700
and a crucial spot
for the nation's defense.

395
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,910
Huh.

396
00:18:01,870 --> 00:18:03,920
It's essentially
like taking a blade

397
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:05,750
and putting it to the throat

398
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:08,550
of the First Capital
and Galtuile Fortress.

399
00:18:11,970 --> 00:18:13,550
-[people screaming]
-She killed someone

400
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:14,640
in her own family.

401
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,090
And high up
in the Temple, as well.

402
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:17,850
[SIENA] Excuse me!
We need to get through!

403
00:18:17,890 --> 00:18:19,020
[Siena, Zofflec gasp]

404
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:21,600
[MAN 1] How could you kill
High Priest Marlen?

405
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,270
[MAN 2] You deserve
a painful death.

406
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,940
-Filthy heretic!
-Make her suffer!

407
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,270
[MALE SOLDIER] Go on.
Keep moving.

408
00:18:28,610 --> 00:18:29,730
Captain Kivia.

409
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:30,860
How did this happen?

410
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,660
[people booing, exclaiming]

411
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:42,620
[MALE INSPECTOR]
Patausche Kivia,

412
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:45,080
Captain of the Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights.

413
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:47,920
Why did you kill
High Priest Marlen Kivia

414
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,420
and Infantry Lieutenant
Rajit Heathrow?

415
00:18:51,050 --> 00:18:53,510
You can keep asking,
but it's the same answer.

416
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:56,470
-He was a coexistent and I--
-Liar!

417
00:18:57,140 --> 00:18:58,600
You clearly feared and coveted

418
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:01,140
High Priest Marlen's
popularity and skill.

419
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,480
So you betrayed humanity,

420
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:05,140
killing him and your lieutenant.

421
00:19:05,190 --> 00:19:06,400
-[grunts]
-[chains clinking]

422
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,810
[MALE INSPECTOR] All you need
to do is confess

423
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:09,820
to the undeniable facts.

424
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:12,030
And I will release you
without delay.

425
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,740
What's going to happen
to my knights?

426
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,830
And the hero unit.

427
00:19:19,870 --> 00:19:22,160
Where are Xylo Forbartz
and the others?

428
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:26,420
Why aren't you
holding a proper trial?

429
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:28,920
Let me speak in a court of law!

430
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,630
It seems you need more time
to think it through.

431
00:19:34,670 --> 00:19:36,760
You'll come around eventually.

432
00:19:37,590 --> 00:19:38,720
[grunts]

433
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:42,430
[rain pouring]

434
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:50,310
[mouse squeaks]

435
00:19:55,650 --> 00:19:57,240
[footsteps approaching]

436
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:00,910
[KAFZEN] Forgive
my late arrival.

437
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:04,240
The discussion took a fair bit
of time to conclude.

438
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:05,750
[chains clinking]

439
00:20:05,790 --> 00:20:08,830
We weren't positive
that we could add one more.

440
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,580
It was a difficult decision.

441
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:16,470
[ENFIÉ] Hmm.

442
00:20:19,970 --> 00:20:21,100
[sighs]

443
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,600
You're Patausche Kivia.

444
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:24,810
Formerly,

445
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:27,060
captain of the Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights.

446
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:29,020
Your abilities
on the battlefield

447
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:30,230
are exceptional,

448
00:20:30,650 --> 00:20:33,860
but it was your mental fortitude
that caught us by surprise.

449
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:34,940
You killed a relative

450
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:37,700
-to whom you owe a great deal.
-[Kivia gasps]

451
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:39,700
[KAFZEN] You mercilessly
took the life

452
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,870
of someone you deeply respected,

453
00:20:42,370 --> 00:20:44,740
for the sake
of complete strangers,

454
00:20:44,790 --> 00:20:47,290
making it an action
that transcended any notion

455
00:20:47,330 --> 00:20:49,080
of self-interest.

456
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:52,000
You have
the unbridled conviction

457
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,340
of a savior,

458
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:57,550
or perhaps more accurately,
the delusion of one.

459
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:00,720
How do you know all that?

460
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:03,800
[KAFZEN] My goddess
has the ability to summon books.

461
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:08,100
In other words, you might say
she can summon information.

462
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:09,440
-[ENFIÉ] Hmm.
-[KAFZEN] Hmm?

463
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:14,190
Ah? No, Enfié.
I haven’t forgotten.

464
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:17,030
-Thank you.
-[chuckles]

465
00:21:17,070 --> 00:21:18,740
-[chains clinking]
-What is this?

466
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:22,360
-Are you a Holy Knight?
-[KAFZEN] Hmm?

467
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:27,290
I am. A knight
of the Twelfth Order.

468
00:21:27,830 --> 00:21:29,790
Which means we
were once associates,

469
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:32,420
though I know
it seems farfetched.

470
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:36,710
I have come here
to offer you the chance

471
00:21:36,750 --> 00:21:38,210
to choose your own fate.

472
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:40,010
You have only two options.

473
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:42,970
The first, you can be executed

474
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,550
as a member of the coexisters.

475
00:21:46,470 --> 00:21:50,020
The second,
you can become a penal hero

476
00:21:50,060 --> 00:21:52,440
and continue fighting
against the Demon Blight.

477
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:53,560
[Kivia gasps]

478
00:21:54,270 --> 00:21:55,900
[chuckles]

479
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:58,650
Heroes are denied
the sweet release of death

480
00:21:58,690 --> 00:22:00,740
and have no freedom whatsoever.

481
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:03,030
It's a life without glory,

482
00:22:03,070 --> 00:22:04,660
devoted to helping others.

483
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:06,530
Those nameless strangers.

484
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:09,290
I wouldn't agree
to such a thing myself.

485
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:12,920
And to be frank, I don't believe
you're cut out for it, either.

486
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:14,880
What are they?

487
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:18,420
What is the hero penalty really?

488
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,090
[sighs]

489
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:25,140
I'd be more than happy
to tell you everything I can.

490
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:26,640
I take it
you've heard the rumors

491
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,010
floating around town.

492
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:30,390
The ones
about our first goddess

493
00:22:30,430 --> 00:22:33,520
and her ability
to summon heroic champions.

494
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:37,360
Long ago, at the beginning
of the first war,

495
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:40,320
she called forth warriors
from other worlds.

496
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:42,780
But the cultural differences

497
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:44,610
made it hard to communicate.

498
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:48,780
And so, those in charge

499
00:22:48,830 --> 00:22:50,870
changed their tactics
accordingly.

500
00:22:51,450 --> 00:22:53,750
They summoned the dead
of this world

501
00:22:54,290 --> 00:22:56,830
and deployed them
as their champions instead.

502
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:02,130
They summoned the dead
of this world.

503
00:23:02,170 --> 00:23:03,550
Then,

504
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,800
the resurrections.

505
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:06,760
You're remarkably clever.

506
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,890
Heroes stand
on the front lines

507
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:12,100
in the battle
against the Demon Blight,

508
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,350
and are denied
even the dignity of death

509
00:23:14,390 --> 00:23:16,350
in this endless war.

510
00:23:18,190 --> 00:23:20,190
[KIVIA] So
that's what heroes are.

511
00:23:21,730 --> 00:23:23,110
I can't believe it.

512
00:23:23,650 --> 00:23:25,610
I'm afraid it's true.

513
00:23:25,650 --> 00:23:26,820
And I'll bet you're wondering

514
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:29,030
how it became
a criminal sentence.

515
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:30,530
Just take my word for it.

516
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:33,040
We have our reasons
for that one as well.

517
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:34,160
By the way,

518
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:38,000
the first goddess' power
is incredible, but flawed.

519
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:39,790
I believe you're already aware

520
00:23:40,090 --> 00:23:43,420
of what happens to a person
after too many resurrections.

521
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:44,550
[gasps]

522
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:49,800
They lose their memories
little by little.

523
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:53,470
And their sense of self
is worn away.

524
00:23:54,560 --> 00:23:57,520
Yes, and humans apparently
do possess something similar

525
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,270
to the concept of a soul.

526
00:23:59,310 --> 00:24:01,070
The results
are meaningfully affected

527
00:24:01,110 --> 00:24:03,530
by how clearly
she remembers the target.

528
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,740
It impacts precision

529
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:09,410
both in regard
to summoning and resurrection.

530
00:24:09,450 --> 00:24:11,870
Though, we do have Enfié.

531
00:24:12,370 --> 00:24:13,660
Her records are a boon.

532
00:24:14,250 --> 00:24:16,370
The first goddess
expends all of her energy

533
00:24:16,410 --> 00:24:17,870
on a single task.

534
00:24:18,420 --> 00:24:20,750
Every day,
she must remember the heroes

535
00:24:20,790 --> 00:24:22,090
and their memories.

536
00:24:22,710 --> 00:24:24,880
Yet her mind has a limit.

537
00:24:25,340 --> 00:24:28,840
I'd say she has room
for just one more hero.

538
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,720
[KIVIA] Humanity's trump card.

539
00:24:32,890 --> 00:24:35,850
But are you certain
it's worth such a heavy cost?

540
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:39,940
Interesting question.

541
00:24:40,690 --> 00:24:42,190
It is my sincerest hope

542
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:45,150
that the answer turns out
to be a resounding yes.

543
00:24:45,940 --> 00:24:48,450
Those are all the secrets
I can disclose.

544
00:24:48,900 --> 00:24:50,610
I'll leave
the sacred-seal collar

545
00:24:50,660 --> 00:24:52,700
and "repairs" for another day.

546
00:24:55,040 --> 00:24:56,120
It's time.

547
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:58,160
Make your choice,

548
00:24:58,540 --> 00:25:00,580
Patausche Kivia.

549
00:25:06,210 --> 00:25:07,420
[KIVIA] Huh.

550
00:25:08,170 --> 00:25:10,130
If I agree to be a hero,

551
00:25:11,340 --> 00:25:14,810
does that mean
you'll get me out of this cell?

552
00:25:14,850 --> 00:25:16,310
[KAFZEN] Of course.

553
00:25:16,350 --> 00:25:19,770
But you'll have to die
before we can begin.

554
00:25:20,190 --> 00:25:22,560
Then I'll carry you out
of here in pieces.

555
00:25:23,190 --> 00:25:25,730
There's no room for compromise.

556
00:25:25,770 --> 00:25:28,070
Put your faith
in the goddess and die.

557
00:25:28,490 --> 00:25:30,240
Or refuse to and die.

558
00:25:30,860 --> 00:25:33,530
Those are the only options
you have.

559
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:36,790
[♪ pensive music playing]

560
00:25:37,620 --> 00:25:39,410
[KIVIA] Fate is cruel.

561
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:41,750
Born to a family of priests.

562
00:25:42,210 --> 00:25:43,580
I needed to escape.

563
00:25:44,210 --> 00:25:47,130
My uncle was the only one
who understood me.

564
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:51,470
And now I've killed him.

565
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:55,930
Left alone in this dark,

566
00:25:55,970 --> 00:25:57,470
I keep wondering.

567
00:25:58,060 --> 00:25:59,930
What do my knights think of me?

568
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:02,140
And the hero unit,

569
00:26:02,190 --> 00:26:04,310
what do they make of my crime?

570
00:26:05,690 --> 00:26:08,860
I hope they'll chalk it up
to a fit of madness

571
00:26:08,900 --> 00:26:12,610
because if they hate me
for what I have done...

572
00:26:13,030 --> 00:26:14,030
[sobs]

573
00:26:14,660 --> 00:26:18,330
...if they believe what's said
about me being a coexister

574
00:26:18,370 --> 00:26:20,040
and betraying humanity.

575
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:22,120
[continues sobbing]

576
00:26:24,170 --> 00:26:25,920
If my knights...

577
00:26:27,630 --> 00:26:29,630
If he were to think that
of me...

578
00:26:31,970 --> 00:26:34,300
[continues sobbing]

579
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:36,930
...I couldn't bear it!

580
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:45,230
Well, so be it.

581
00:26:46,810 --> 00:26:50,900
I suppose that if this
will allow me to keep fighting,

582
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:54,110
then I have no choice.

583
00:26:54,150 --> 00:26:56,990
For all those faceless strangers
I'll never meet,

584
00:26:57,450 --> 00:26:58,870
I swear to fight.

585
00:27:00,910 --> 00:27:02,540
I'll be a hero.

586
00:27:02,580 --> 00:27:04,580
[♪ tense music playing]

587
00:27:13,510 --> 00:27:14,760
[KAFZEN] I had a feeling.

588
00:27:15,220 --> 00:27:17,640
There's no going back on this.

589
00:27:18,050 --> 00:27:19,680
And I don't recommend it.

590
00:27:20,220 --> 00:27:23,020
But I will make certain
this remains a secret.

591
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,020
On a personal level,

592
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:30,150
I am still vehemently opposed
to making you a hero.

593
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,360
That said,

594
00:27:33,940 --> 00:27:37,530
I feel it's my responsibility
to respect your oath.

595
00:27:38,620 --> 00:27:39,660
Go on.

596
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:40,950
There's no time to waste.

597
00:27:47,580 --> 00:27:49,130
[chain clinking]

598
00:27:59,140 --> 00:28:01,560
In sacrifice to the lives
of the many,

599
00:28:02,010 --> 00:28:05,430
you have come to this moment,
and I bear witness.

600
00:28:06,270 --> 00:28:07,730
[panting]

601
00:28:07,770 --> 00:28:09,810
[KAFZEN] Patausche Kivia,

602
00:28:09,860 --> 00:28:13,360
it is time I sentence you
to be...

603
00:28:14,230 --> 00:28:15,530
a hero.

604
00:28:15,570 --> 00:28:16,900
[clinking]

605
00:28:21,330 --> 00:28:23,580
[♪ closing theme song playing]

606
00:29:26,100 --> 00:29:29,770
SENTENCED TO BE A HERO
